### Exercise catalog
#
# Requires the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
# Send one of the logins in section 1 first - every request below reads its token
# from that named response.
#
# Preconditions:
#   docker compose --profile full up -d
#   seed data from db/src/main.sql
#
# Seeded ownership (63 global entries plus one per user):
#   user 2 max        -> 'Slow Tempo Push-Up'
#   user 3 lena_lifts -> 'Zone 2 Treadmill Run'
#   user 4 marco      -> one own exercise
#   user 5 sina       -> one own exercise, soft deleted (deleted_at set)

@host = http://localhost:8080
@frontend = http://localhost:3000
###############################################################################
###############################################################################
# 1  Logins
###############################################################################
###############################################################################

### 1.1  Log in as max
# @name loginMax
POST {{host}}/backend/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "max",
  "password": "password"
}

### 1.2  Log in as lena_lifts
# @name loginLena
POST {{host}}/backend/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "lena_lifts",
  "password": "password"
}

### 1.3  Log in as sina (exercise is soft deleted)
# @name loginSina
POST {{host}}/backend/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "sina",
  "password": "password"
}

###############################################################################
###############################################################################
# 2  The catalog is user-scoped
###############################################################################
###############################################################################

# Same endpoint, different token, different result. This is what the whole auth
# setup buys: ownership is decided server-side, never by the client.

### 2.1  max -> 64 entries, one of them "Slow Tempo Push-Up" with "custom": true
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 2.2  lena_lifts -> also 64, but her own entry is "Zone 2 Treadmill Run"
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLena.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 2.3  sina -> 63, because her own exercise carries a deleted_at
# Proves the soft delete filter, not just the ownership filter.
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{loginSina.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
###############################################################################
# 3  Access control
###############################################################################
###############################################################################

### 3.1  No token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises

### 3.2  Refresh token instead of an access token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
# Test for the token type validator (see http/auth.http section 3)
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.refreshToken}}

###############################################################################
###############################################################################
# 4  Detail view of a single exercise
###############################################################################
###############################################################################

# Seeded ids: 1-63 global, 64 max, 65 lena_lifts, 66 marco,
# 67 sina (soft deleted).

### 4.1  A global exercise -> 200, "custom": false
# Visible to every user because owner_user_id is NULL.
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises/1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 4.2  max reads his own exercise -> 200 "Slow Tempo Push-Up", "custom": true
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises/64
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 4.3  lena_lifts reads her own exercise -> 200 "Zone 2 Treadmill Run"
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises/65
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLena.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
###############################################################################
# 5  The detail view is ownership scoped
###############################################################################
###############################################################################

# The three requests below must return an identical body. Any difference between
# them would tell a caller which ids exist behind exercises they cannot read.

### 5.1  max asks for lena's exercise -> 404 EXERCISE_NOT_FOUND
# Deliberately not 403: a 403 would confirm that id 65 exists.
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises/65
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 5.2  sina asks for her own, soft deleted exercise -> 404 EXERCISE_NOT_FOUND
# She is the owner, so this covers the deleted_at filter rather than ownership.
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises/67
Authorization: Bearer {{loginSina.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 5.3  An id that was never seeded -> 404 EXERCISE_NOT_FOUND
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
###############################################################################
# 6  Detail view access control and malformed paths
###############################################################################
###############################################################################

### 6.1  No token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
# The filter chain rejects the request before the controller is reached.
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises/1

### 6.2  Refresh token instead of an access token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises/1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.refreshToken}}

### 6.3  Non-numeric id -> 400, but NOT in the ErrorResponse shape
# /{id} matches and only the conversion to Long fails, so this is a
# MethodArgumentTypeMismatchException with no handler of ours behind it.
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 6.4  Trailing slash -> 404 RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND, not EXERCISE_NOT_FOUND
# Spring 6 no longer matches a trailing slash, so no handler is found at all.
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises/1/
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 6.5  A negative id -> 404 EXERCISE_NOT_FOUND
# Long parses fine, the query simply finds nothing.
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises/-1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
###############################################################################
# 7  To-Do/WIP
###############################################################################
###############################################################################
# Kept here so the gaps stay visible while the frontend is built against this.

### 7.1  The detail view still returns the list shape (verified)
# instructions and the muscle groups are not exposed yet; both belong in a
# dedicated ExerciseDetailResponse. Section 4 covers what is served today.

### 7.2  Filtering by type -> silently ignored, all 64 come back (verified)
# Worth knowing before the frontend starts relying on it.
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises?exerciseType=CARDIO
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 7.3  Filtering by muscle group -> also ignored; the join table is not mapped yet
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises?muscleGroupId=3
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 7.4  Creating a custom exercise -> 405, no write endpoint exists
# Note the body: 405 still comes from Spring's error dispatch, so it carries
# {timestamp,status,error,path} rather than the ErrorResponse shape every other
# error uses. A handler for HttpRequestMethodNotSupportedException would fix it.
POST {{host}}/backend/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "My Own Movement",
  "exerciseType": "STRENGTH",
  "description": "Added from the REST client."
}

###############################################################################
# 8  Resetting tokens
###############################################################################
# There is no request that clears the tokens of this file. Every request above
# carries its own token, read from the login response it names, so there is no
# ambient session to end:
#
#   * To replace a token, send its login in section 1 again - the named response
#     is overwritten.
#   * To drop all of them, reload the VS Code window; the response variables
#     live in memory only.
#   * A token cannot be revoked server-side yet. /backend/auth/logout does not
#     exist (see http/auth.http section 6), so every token issued stays valid
#     until it expires: 15 minutes for access, 7 days for refresh.
#
# What can be cleared is the browser session behind the frontend routes.

### 8.1  Clear the frontend cookies -> 200 {"success": true}
# Deletes access_token and refresh_token for the browser, which is what
# /exercises and /dashboard read. Requires the frontend on port 3000.
POST {{frontend}}/api/logout

### 8.2  Which user does a token belong to?
# No whoami endpoint exists. The catalog answers it indirectly: the entry with
# "custom": true is the caller's own. Swap the login name to check another one.
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMax.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 8.3  An empty token -> 401 UNAUTHENTICATED
# What a cleared token would look like on the wire. Useful to confirm that a 200
# above really came from a token and not from a gap in the filter chain.
GET {{host}}/backend/exercises
Authorization: Bearer
